## 16. Observability — TruLens + Langsmith

### Purpose

Two complementary observability layers run alongside the platform:

| Tool          | Primary role                                                              |
|---------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **Langsmith** | Trace every LLM call end-to-end: inputs, outputs, latency, token cost    |
| **TruLens**   | Evaluate prompt quality and LLM output correctness against defined metrics |

Neither tool is in the critical path. If either is unavailable or disabled, the review pipeline runs
normally. Observability is a side-channel, never a gate.

### Langsmith — LLM call tracing

#### What it traces

Every call through `LLMProvider.complete()` is wrapped in a Langsmith run:

```
Run
├── agent_id
├── prompt_version_id
├── provider + model
├── rendered system prompt
├── rendered user message
├── raw LLM response
├── parsed structured output
├── input_tokens / output_tokens
├── latency_ms
├── status (success | error)
└── review_run_id  (links back to the platform's own audit trail)
```

#### Integration point

Langsmith tracing is added in `llm/provider.py` at the `LLMProvider` base class level — not in
individual providers or agents. One decorator/wrapper, all providers traced automatically.

```python
# llm/provider.py  (illustrative — exact SDK calls may vary)
from langsmith import traceable

class LLMProvider(ABC):
    @traceable(name="llm_complete", run_type="llm")
    def complete(self, prompt: str, schema: dict | None = None, **kwargs) -> dict:
        return self._complete(prompt, schema, **kwargs)

    @abstractmethod
    def _complete(self, prompt: str, schema: dict | None = None, **kwargs) -> dict:
        ...
```

#### `.env` configuration

```dotenv
# ── Langsmith ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LANGSMITH_ENABLED=true
LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=true
LANGCHAIN_API_KEY=<your-langsmith-key>
LANGCHAIN_PROJECT=ib-ppt-validator
LANGCHAIN_ENDPOINT=https://api.smith.langchain.com
```

Set `LANGSMITH_ENABLED=false` to disable tracing with zero code changes. When disabled, the wrapper
is a no-op.

#### What the Langsmith UI gives you

- Full prompt + response for every LLM call, searchable by `review_run_id` or `agent_id`
- Token usage and cost trends per agent and per prompt version
- Latency percentiles per provider
- Error rate per agent
- Side-by-side comparison of two prompt versions on the same input

### TruLens — prompt evaluation and correctness

#### What it evaluates

TruLens runs **asynchronous evaluation jobs** against completed agent runs. It does not block the
review pipeline. Evaluations are triggered after a run completes and results are stored separately.

| Metric                  | Description                                                        | Applies to              |
|-------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------|
| `answer_relevance`      | Is the finding relevant to the slide content?                      | All LLM agents          |
| `groundedness`          | Is the finding grounded in the actual slide text (not hallucinated)? | All LLM agents        |
| `context_relevance`     | Is the retrieved context (slide content) relevant to the prompt?   | All LLM agents          |
| `coherence`             | Is the finding description coherent and well-formed?               | All LLM agents          |
| `requirement_coverage`  | Does the agent output cover all requirements in the proposal context? | Proposal Agent only   |
| `contradiction_detection` | Does the agent correctly identify contradictions?               | Proposal Agent, Critic  |
| `output_schema_compliance` | Does the output conform to the declared output schema?         | All LLM agents          |

#### Integration point

TruLens evaluation is triggered from `ObservabilityService` after each agent run completes:

```python
# services/observability_service.py
class ObservabilityService:
    def record_agent_run(self, agent_run: AgentRun) -> None:
        """Write to audit DB. If TruLens enabled, enqueue async eval job."""

    def evaluate_async(self, agent_run: AgentRun, prompt_version: PromptVersion) -> None:
        """
        Run TruLens feedback functions against agent_run.
        Store results in trulens_evaluations table.
        Never called in the critical path — always async/background.
        """
```

#### DB table for evaluation results

```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS trulens_evaluations (
    id                  INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    agent_run_id        INTEGER NOT NULL,
    prompt_version_id   INTEGER NOT NULL,
    metric              TEXT NOT NULL,      -- e.g. "groundedness"
    score               REAL,              -- 0.0 – 1.0
    explanation         TEXT,
    evaluated_at        DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);
```

Additive migration, idempotent.

#### `.env` configuration

```dotenv
# ── TruLens ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
TRULENS_ENABLED=true
TRULENS_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///trulens.db   # or postgres DSN for production
TRULENS_EVAL_PROVIDER=openai               # provider TruLens uses for its own evals
TRULENS_EVAL_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini             # cheap model is fine for eval
```

Set `TRULENS_ENABLED=false` to disable all evaluation jobs with zero code changes.

### Prompt evaluation workflow

When a new prompt version is created and before it is activated in production:

```
1. Author creates new prompt version (status: draft) in Admin UI
2. Author clicks "Run Evaluation" in Admin UI
3. Platform runs the draft prompt against the golden evaluation dataset
   (a set of known PPT + expected findings pairs)
4. TruLens scores the outputs on all applicable metrics
5. Scores appear in Admin UI alongside the previous active version's scores
6. Author compares: if new version scores better, activate it
7. Langsmith shows the full trace for every eval call
```

This makes prompt improvement a measurable, evidence-based process rather than guesswork.

### Observability Admin UI

The React Admin UI must expose an Observability section:

| Screen                  | Content                                                              |
|-------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Agent Run Dashboard     | All runs, scores, latency, token cost, status — filterable by agent |
| LLM Call Explorer       | Langsmith-linked trace per call; prompt in / response out           |
| Prompt Eval Results     | TruLens scores per prompt version per metric, with trend chart      |
| Prompt Version Compare  | Side-by-side metric scores for any two prompt versions              |
| Alerts                  | Groundedness < threshold, error rate spike, latency regression      |

### Failure behaviour

- Langsmith unreachable → log WARNING, continue. No finding is lost, no run is blocked.
- TruLens eval job fails → log WARNING, mark evaluation row as `status: failed`. Review run is
  unaffected.
- Neither tool writes to the critical `agent_run` or `findings` tables — they are read-only consumers
  of the audit trail.

### `.env` — complete observability block

```dotenv
# ── Observability ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Langsmith
LANGSMITH_ENABLED=true
LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=true
LANGCHAIN_API_KEY=<your-langsmith-key>
LANGCHAIN_PROJECT=ib-ppt-validator
LANGCHAIN_ENDPOINT=https://api.smith.langchain.com

# TruLens
TRULENS_ENABLED=true
TRULENS_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///trulens.db
TRULENS_EVAL_PROVIDER=openai
TRULENS_EVAL_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
```

### Implementation checklist

- [ ] `ObservabilityService` in `services/observability_service.py`
- [ ] Langsmith `@traceable` wrapper on `LLMProvider.complete()` (base class, not per-provider)
- [ ] `LANGSMITH_ENABLED` guard — no-op when false
- [ ] TruLens feedback functions: `answer_relevance`, `groundedness`, `context_relevance`,
      `coherence`, `output_schema_compliance`
- [ ] Additional TruLens functions: `requirement_coverage`, `contradiction_detection` for Proposal Agent
- [ ] `trulens_evaluations` DB table (additive migration)
- [ ] Async eval job triggered from `ObservabilityService.record_agent_run()`
- [ ] `TRULENS_ENABLED` guard — no-op when false
- [ ] Golden evaluation dataset for prompt testing (separate from unit tests)
- [ ] Admin UI: Agent Run Dashboard, LLM Call Explorer, Prompt Eval Results, Version Compare, Alerts
- [ ] `.env.example` updated with all observability vars
- [ ] Unit tests: observability disabled path (both flags false) — pipeline must run identically
